@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-round-long-rental-discount-to-nearest-cent
+type: decision-log
+title: "Round long-rental discount to nearest cent"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+A rental of `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS` (3) days or more now costs 10% less than its full price
+(`days * dailyPrice`), for both `quote` and `book`. `dailyPrice` and `total` are integer euro cents
+(enforced by `addEquipment`), but `fullPrice * 0.9` is not always a whole number (e.g. 7503 cents * 0.9 =
+6752.7).
+
+## Decision
+
+Compute the discounted total as `Math.round(fullPrice * (1 - LONG_RENTAL_DISCOUNT))` in a new `priceFor`
+helper, shared by `quote` and `book` through `resolveQuote`, instead of truncating or introducing a
+fixed-point/decimal type. Round-half-away-from-zero on a non-negative amount matches how a cash till
+would settle a fraction of a cent, and keeps the module dependency-free. The threshold and rate are named
+constants (`LONG_RENTAL_DAYS`, `LONG_RENTAL_DISCOUNT`) rather than inline literals, so the policy is
+stated once and can't drift between `quote` and `book`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `total` stays an integer number of cents for every rental, discounted or not, matching the existing
+  `Quote`/`Booking` contract.
+- Two different `dailyPrice`/duration combinations that produce the same fractional full price round the
+  same way, since rounding happens once, in one helper, after the discount is applied — not per day.
+- If the discount ever needs a different rounding rule (e.g. always round in the customer's favour), only
+  `priceFor` changes; `resolveQuote`, `quote` and `book` are unaffected.
