@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: task-003-discount-rentals-of-3-days-by-10
+type: task
+title: "Discount rentals of 3+ days by 10%"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+A rental of 3 days or more now costs 10% less than its full price. Quotes and bookings both show the
+reduced total.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added a `priceFor(days, dailyPrice)` helper in `src/index.ts` that returns the full price
+  (`days * dailyPrice`) unchanged for fewer than `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS` (3) days, and
+  `Math.round(fullPrice * (1 - LONG_RENTAL_DISCOUNT))` (10% off, rounded to the nearest cent) from 3 days
+  on. See dl-004 for the rounding rationale.
+- `resolveQuote` now calls `priceFor` instead of computing `days * item.dailyPrice` directly, so both
+  `quote` and `book` (which both go through `resolveQuote`) apply the same discount rule.
+- Test-first: added failing tests for a sub-3-day quote (no discount), an exactly-3-day quote, a
+  longer-than-3-day quote, a fractional-cent case that exercises rounding, and a 3-day booking, then
+  implemented `priceFor` to turn them green.
+- Updated the pre-existing `'quotes a multi-day rental in integer cents'` test, which used a 3-day
+  period and asserted the old (now-discounted) full price; shortened it to 2 days so it still
+  characterizes plain multi-day pricing without overlapping the new discount tests.
+- `npm test`: 19/19 passing.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- None identified; the discount threshold and rate are named constants in `src/index.ts` if they ever
+  need to change.
